I have successfully fixed all 10 failing tests across the 3 modules in `src/` without modifying any test files or skipping any tests.

### Changes Summary

1. **`src/auth.py`**
   - Updated `has_permission` to perform a case-insensitive check by converting both user roles and the required role to lowercase.
   - Fixed `is_admin_or_owner` to correctly use logical `or` instead of `and` so that matching either the admin role OR the owner ID grants access.

2. **`src/inventory.py`**
   - Corrected class instantiation to avoid mutable default sharing by deep-copying `initial` into a new dictionary `self._stock = dict(initial)`.
   - Modified `add` to accumulate quantity for existing SKUs rather than overwriting.
   - Corrected `reserve` boundary checking so users can reserve up to the exact available quantity (`qty > self.available(sku)`).
   - Added validation in `release` to raise a `ValueError` if attempting to release more than the quantity currently reserved.

3. **`src/text_utils.py`**
   - Added lowercasing of `text` at the start of `slugify`.
   - Used regular expression `re.sub(r"-+", "-", collapsed)` in `slugify` to properly collapse consecutive hyphens into a single hyphen.
   - Corrected length truncation in `truncate` to account for the actual length of the suffix, slicing the text to `max(0, max_len - len(suffix))`.

All 15 tests in the suite are now passing cleanly.
